{"name":"Friendly Basilisk","hex":"#e2f5e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"friendly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Generally warm, approachable and easy to relate with in character.","Inviting, characteristic of friendliness."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A game which is of no consequence in terms of ranking, betting, etc.","A person or entity on the same side as one's own in a conflict."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendly"},{"term":"basilisk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical snake-like dragon, so venomous that even its gaze is deadly.","A type of dragon used in heraldry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suggesting a basilisk (snake-like dragon): baleful, spellbinding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basilisk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Basilisk","blocks":[{"text":"In ancient European bestiaries and folklore, a basilisk is a legendary reptile reputed to be a serpent king, who causes any being to die when glanced at. According to the Naturalis Historia of Pliny the Elder, the basilisk of Cyrene is a small snake, \"being not more than twelve inches in length\", that is so venomous, it leaves a wide trail of deadly venom in its path, its gaze likewise just as lethal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Basilisk_aldrovandi.jpg/330px-Basilisk_aldrovandi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilisk","wikidata":"Q152519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sint_Michael_Zwolle_Stadszegel_1295.jpg/330px-Sint_Michael_Zwolle_Stadszegel_1295.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sint_Michael_Zwolle_Stadszegel_1295.jpg/330px-Sint_Michael_Zwolle_Stadszegel_1295.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser